      answer: 'On Windows XP laptops, the song contained one of the natural resonant frequencies of a model of 5400 rpm laptop hard drive, so the sound made the drive (even in a nearby laptop) fail and the machine crash. The manufacturer added a custom filter in the audio pipeline that detected and removed the offending frequencies.',
      points: ['Windows XP laptops', 'song hit a resonant frequency of 5400 rpm hard drives', 'could crash a nearby laptop too', 'fix: audio-pipeline filter removing those frequencies'],
      why: 'Answers "can you crash someone else\'s computer without touching it?" It was later registered as CVE-2022-38392.',
